  "[action] (to Wang Lung) the eldest son and the second son return to the land",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"I have bought an old man for a slave to work in the fields, and there is an old man from my village in a house of one room near me. He has an old woman for his wife and they have two children, a boy and a girl, who are too young to work. I have told them that they may live for my pleasure for a few years and they will have their food and their clothes and their beds and their bedding while I am alive.\"",
  "[action] (to Wang Lung) the eldest son and the second son return to the land",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and who will work in the fields?\"",
